$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of D-mannitol (3.0 g, 16 mmol), 2-butanone (4.4 mL, 49 mmol),
triethyl orthoformate (2.7 mL, 16 mmol), BF3·Et2O (0.2 mL, 1.6 mmol) and
dry DMSO (6.4 mL) was stirred for 22 h at rt. The mixture was then poured
into 15 mL of 10% ice-cooled NaHCO3 solution and was extracted with Et2O
(10 mL × 3). The organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and concentrated in
vacuo. To a solution of the residue obtained in 55 mL of Et2O was added a
solution of NaIO4 (4.1 g, 19 mmol) and Bu4NF (0.12 mL, 0.4 mmol) in 2.1
mL of water, and the mixture was stirred for 6 h at rt. The mixture was
separated and aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (15 mL × 3). The
combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
2.1 g (91%) of a red oil (mixture of D-aldehydes).
