$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure of the protection of
aldehyde with alcohol in the presence of ATPB. To a solution of
3-phenylpropanal (1) (287 mg, 2.14 mmol) in 2 mL of methanol was added
ATPB (85 mg, 0.21 mmol) and the solution was stirred at RT. The reaction
was complete in 20 min. The solution was concentrated and the residue was
chromatographed on silica gel to give the desired product 1a (358.8 mg,
1.99 mmol) in 93% yield. Cyclohexanecarboxaldehyde dimethyl acetal (2a),
yield 90%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 0.97-1.23 (m, 5H), 1.58-1.79 (m,
6H), 3.33 (s, 6H, -OCH3), 3.99 (d, J = 7.2Hz, 1H, -CH(OCH3)2). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 25.1, 26.4 28.0, 40.0, 53.5 (1°, -OCH3), 108.5 (3°,
-CH(OCH3)2). IR (KBr) 2912, 1452, 1378cm-1.MS m/z (relative intensity):
158 (M+, 4), 154 (100), 136 (74), 117 (37).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative method using solid-supported catalyst,
acetonyltriphenylphosphonium bromide supported on polystyrene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Acetonyltriphenylphosphonium Bromide and Its Polymer-Supported Analogues
as Catalysts for the Protection of Carbonyl Compounds as Acetals or
Thioacetals
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
