$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Dimethyl Acetal under Solvent-Free Conditions;
4-Methylbenzaldehyde Dimethyl Acetal; Typical Procedure (Method A) To a
magnetically stirred mixture of 4-methybenzaldehyde (0.3 g, 2.5 mmol) and
TMOF (0.29 g, 2.75 mmol, 1.1 equiv) was added HClO4-SiO2 (25 mg, 0.012
mmol, 0.5 mol%) and the mixture was stirred at 25-30 °C until complete
consumption of the aldehyde (10 min, TLC). The mixture was diluted with
EtOAc (2 mL), filtered through a plug of cotton (to separate the
catalyst), and the cotton plug was washed with EtOAc (2 × 1 mL). The
combined EtOAc filtrates were concentrated on a rotary evaporator to
afford 4-methylbenzaldehyde dimethyl acetal identical (spectral data)
with an authentic sample.6a Table 1, entry 17, yield 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Perchloric acid adsorbed on silica gel (HClO4-SiO2) as an inexpensive,
extremely efficient, and reusable dual catalyst system for acetal/ketal
formation and their deprotection to aldehydes/ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kumar, Raj; Kumar, Dinesh; Chakraborti, Asit K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2007), (2), 299-303

