$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Carboxy-6-methoxy-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphtbalene (9a) from the Acetal
(7a); Typical Procedure: A mixture of the crude α -bromo ketone 6a, (0.19
g, 0.7 mmol), trimethyl orthoformate (0.15mL, 1.4mmoI), methanol (1 mL)
and p-toluenesulfonic acid (0,005 g) is stirred at 40 X for 10 h under
nitrogen. The reaction mixture is cooled, poured into saturated aqueous
Na2CO3, (50 mL). and extracted with ether (3 x 20 mL). Work-up of the
extract as given in the literature 3 furnishes the crude α -bromo acetal
7a. Yield, 0.2 g 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Lewis acid-promoted Favorskii-type ring contraction of some cyclic
α-bromo ketones and their acetals
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Maiti, Swaraj B.; Chaudhuri, S. R. Ray; Chatterjee, Amareshwar
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1987), (9), 806-9

