$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Acetalization of
Aldehydes : Aldehyde (5 mmol), ethane 1,2-diol (5 mmol) and metal sulfate
(5 mmol) supported on silica gel (1.65 g) were mixed in a pyrex test tube
and subjected to microwave irradiation for 3-6 min. After complete
conversion, as indicated by TLC, the reaction mass was charged directly
on small silica gel column (100-200 mesh) and eluted with
ethylacetate-hexane (2:8) to afford pure acetal. Yield 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Silica gel-supported metallic sulfates catalyzed chemoselective
acetalization of aldehydes under microwave irradiation
