$DATUM Step 3: 6-Bromo-1,4-dioxaspiro[4.5]decane (7) 2-Bromocyclohexanone (10.3
g, 58.0 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was added to a solution of ethylene glycol (3.58
mL, 64.0 mmol, 1.1 equiv) and p-toluenesulfonic acid monohydrate (2.44 g,
12.8 mmol, 0.22 equiv) in toluene (45 mL). Using a Dean-Stark apparatus,
the reaction solution was refluxed at 124 °C until the theoretical amount
of water (ca. 0.95 mL) was collected in the trap (about 4 h). The
reaction mixture was cooled to 25 °C and washed with aq. 2 M NaOH (30 mL)
and H2O (5 x 20 mL). The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4, filtered
and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (SiO2, i-hexane / Et2O = 95:5).
The desired product 7 in 90 % yield as slightly yellow oil (11.4 g, 52.0
mmol). The analytical data were found to match to the literature
reference.2c
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dean-Stark apparatus used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Sc(OTf)3-Catalyzed Addition of Bromomagnesium 2-Vinyloxy Ethoxide to
Various Aldehydes Leading to Protected Aldol Products
