$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis and characterization of methyl
4-(2-phenyl-1,3-dioxolan-2-yl)benzoate (6a).2 A 100 ml round-bottomed
flask was charged with methyl 4-benzoylbenzoate (1 g, 4.2 mmol),
1,2-ethanediol (0.78 g, 12.5 mmol), 50 ml of reagent grade benzene and
p-toluenesulfonic acid monohydrate (16 mg, 0.04 mmol). The flask was
attached to a Dean-Stark apparatus to remove water and the contents
refluxed for 6 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature,
extracted with dichlormethane, the extracts washed with saturated sodium
bicarbonate solution and dried (Na2SO4). Methyl
4-(2-phenyl-1,3-dioxolan-2-yl)benzoate (3.76 mmol, 90%). Mp 102-103 ºC;
υmax 3084, 3061, 3030, 2934, 2887, 1732, 1602, 1453; δH 8.01-7.99 (2H, d,
J 8.4), 7.62-7.59 (2H, d, J 8.4), 7.52-7.46 (2H, dd, J 8.4, 1.8),
7.37-7.29 (3H, m), 4.08-4.07 (4H, d, J 3.3), 3.90 (3H, s); δC 165.9,
142.6, 140.2, 130.8, 129.4, 128.4, 127.8, 126.3, 126.1, 119.1, 64.9,
51.8; HRESIMS: 307.0942 (calcd. for C17H16O4 + Na 307.0946).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dean-Stark apparatus used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chloral Hydrate as a Water Carrier for the Efficient Deprotection of
Acetals, Dithioacetals, and Tetrahydropyranyl Ethers in Organic Solvents
