$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure Bromoaldehyde 1(0.6 mmol) was added to a stirred
solution of 3(0.6 mmol) and aldehyde 2(0.6 mmol) in THF (2 mL) at 0 °C.
After the mixture was stirred for 4-12 h at 0 °C, MeOH (8 mL) was added
and the resulting solution was stirred for additional 1 h at r.t. Then,
aq NaHCO3 (sat., 10 mL) was added. The mixture was extracted with Et2O-
hexane (4:1, three times) and the organic layer was dried over MgSO4 .
The solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure and the residue was
purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel to give the product
Compound 4aa, yield 89%. (anti, major): 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
7.90-7.85 (m, 2 H), 7.31-7.20 (m, 5 H), 7.05-7.00 (m, 2 H), 5.46-5.43 (br
s, 1 H), 4.71 (s, 1 H), 4.54 (d, J= 0.97 Hz, 1 H, OH), 3.59 (s, 3 H),
3.34 (s, 3 H), 1.30 (s, 3 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 147.98,
146.54, 140.46, 128.40, 127.95, 127.55, 126.98, 121.79, 112.74, 77.15,
59.74, 57.49, 51.54, 11.42. HRMS (CI, 200 eV): m/zcalcd for C18H22NO5:
332.1420 [M++1]; found: 332.1501. Anal. Calcd for C18H21NO5: C, 65.24; H,
6.39; N, 4.23. Found: C, 65.28; H, 6.51; N, 4.11.
