$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure B: Catalytic acetalization. To a
mixture of the carbonyl compound (1.5 mmol) in MeOH (HPLC grade, 5 mL),
hydroxylamine hydrochloride (0.15 mmol) and powdered sodium hydroxide
(0.15 mmol) were added in that order. The reaction was stirred for 18 h,
then 3 mL of saturated NH4Cl and 3 mL of H2O were added. The mixture was
extracted with diethyl ether (3 x 10 mL); the combined organic layers
were washed with brine (10 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated by rotary
evaporation. Catalytic procedure: Cyclohexane carboxaldehyde (0.20 mL,
1.7 mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (5.0 mL) and reacted with hydroxylamine
hydrochloride (0.012 g, 0.18 mmol) and powdered sodium hydroxide (0.006
g, 0.15 mmol) according to procedure B above. Catalytic procedure:
Citronellal (0.50 mL, 2.8 mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (9.3 mL) and
reacted with hydroxylamine hydrochloride (0.020 g, 0.29 mmol) and
powdered sodium hydroxide (0.012 g, 0.31 mmol) according to procedure B
above. The acetal (0.484 g, 87%) was isolated as a clear, colorless oil.
Citronellal dimethyl acetal 2e. 1H NMR and IR spectra correlated with
those reported in the literature.[iv]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Method for the selective formation of dimethyl acetals in the presence of
hydroxylamine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mickelsen, Ky J.; Tajc, Chelsea M.; Greenwood, Kevin R.; Browder, Cindy
C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2012), 42(2), 186-194

