$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Electrocataiytical Acetalization of Aliphatic Aldehydes with Methanol or
1,2-Ethanediol; General Procedure: Apparatus: Electrolysis Cell: Typical
three-electrodc electrolyzcr (volume 0.035 dm3) provided with a reflux
condenser. Cathodes: Platinum (3N. Mennica Panstowa. Warszawa),
0.2x0.2x0.02 dm. Anode: Platinum (3N. Mennica Panstowa, Warszawa), 0.2 x
0.2 x 0.02 dm; or carbon (ELS-359, ZEW-Raciborz); 0.35x0.06x0.03 dm. The
anode is placed centrally between the cathodes in a distance of 0.3 cm.
Electrolyte: Sodium p-toluenesulfonatc (0.5 g) in methanol (0.7 mol) or
1,2-ethanediol (0.5 mol). Current density: 5,0 A/dm2. Feeder cable type
ZT-980-3M (Unitra-Cemi); digital multimeter VC-10T (Unitra-Unima);
thermostat U-2/MLW/: magnetic stirrer type 318 (Unipan). Performance: The
aldehyde (0.019 - 0.025 mol, see Table) is added to the cell and the
mixture is clcctrolyzed until 1.5F/mol has been delivered. When methanol
is used, excess methanol is evaporated and the residue distilled in vacuo
(without prior removal of the salt) using a short Vigreux column to give
the acetal. When 1,2-ethanediol is used for acetalization, the reaction
product is poured into water (50 ml) and the acetal extracted with
heptane (3 x 50 ml). The organic extract is washed with water (40 ml),
dried wilh sodium sulfate, and evaporated under reduced pressure. The
remaining cyclic acetal is fractionally distilled. Yield 88%> B.p.
[°C]/torr found: 98-100°C/40; b.p. [°C]/torr reported or Molecular
formula: 180/7607; nD20: 1.4132; I.R. (neat) ν [cm-1]: 1200, 1145,
1130,1120, 1085, 1070; 1H.N.M.R (CCl4/TMSint) δ [ppm]: 4.20 (t, J = 5Hz,
1H); 3.15 (s, 6H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Electrochem
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient electrocatalytical acetalization of aliphatic aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gora, J.; Smigielski, K.; Kula, J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1986), (7), 586-8

