$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Cascade Michael Addition/Cycloketalization.
General Procedure A. To a solution of α,β-unsaturated carbonyl compound
6a or 6b (0.2 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2 mL) was added cyclic 1,3-dicarbonyl
compound 10a-d (0.3 mmol). After 30 min of stirring, the reaction was
quenched by addition of a saturated NaHCO3 solution (1 mL). The organic
layer was collected, and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (3 x
1 mL). The combined organic fractions were washed with brine, dried over
Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified
by flash column chromatography on silica gel (hexane/EtOAc = 1:2) to
afford the desired product (Table 1). Compound 11n.24 General procedure
A; 34 mg, 88% yield; light-yellow oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 5.41
(d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1H), 4.14 (td, J = 8.8, 2.4 Hz, 1H), 3.97 (q, J = 8.8 Hz,
1H), 2.57-2.55 (m, 2H), 2.40-2.34 (m, 5H), 2.06-2.01 (m, 1H), 2.00-1.91
(m, 2H), 1.70-1.60 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 198.6, 169.2,
107.5, 101.1, 68.9, 36.8, 36.7, 28.6, 27.4, 21.0, 18.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, cascade Michael
addition/cycloketalization reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cascade Michael Addition/Cycloketalization of Cyclic 1,3-Dicarbonyl
Compounds: Important Role of the Tethered Alcohol of α,β-Unsaturated
Carbonyl Compounds on Reaction Rate and Regioselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
